<title>HUNGARY: Hungary three-year bond yield rises to 17.42 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary three-year bond yield rises to 17.42 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of Hungary's three-year government bonds was set by auction at 17.42 percent, up from 17.30 percent at an auction on May 8, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BONDS OF THE 2000/E SERIES</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 April 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 May 2000</p>
<p>    Total on offer	    15,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     19,837.96 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	   12,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		15,600 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  17.42 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		   98.25 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi- anually.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
